# Source structure for the residual normalizer in Proposition 1.3.8

The section centralizer C_LT(Ξ_p(L)/O₂(Ξ_p(L))) is solvable from the
earlier structural alternatives and the original N_L(P)-irreducibility
witness. This result does not depend on containment or action properties
of the residual Y. The existing Components leaf supplies all its conditional
C-component and characteristic-normalizer consequences.

Assuming Ξ_p(L) ≤ Y, the Frattini factorization constructs an actual SL₂(r)
section in N_Y(P), retaining the same prime r in the Fitting quotient of
L/O₂(L). The exported result includes r's prime restriction and both
isomorphism assertions. Universal earlier-source implications and the
authorized radical action witness remain parameters; final source assembly
and the containment Ξ_p(L) ≤ Y belong to the parent task.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of Proposition 1.3.8, printed pp.512–513, and A.3.6, pp.43–45.
-/
